 \Sigma_{y}\coloneqq\eta^{-1}\,\mathrm{Cov}(X\mid Y=y) , as in the normalized
coordinates of Appendix  C . Differentiating the
log-density of  \pi_{\eta}^{Y}  gives 
 

 
  
 \nabla U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(y-\bar{x}_{y})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\nabla^{2}U_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}(I-\Sigma_{y})\,. 
  
 (D.10) 
 
 The conditional potential in  x  has Hessian between
 (\alpha+\eta^{-1})I  and  (\beta+\eta^{-1})I . Applying
 Lemma   D.3  in ( D.10 ) gives
( 2.13 ). 

